
## Updated ```unset .gitignore ``` Configuration

```text
# 1. Ignore everything at the root level
/*

# 2. Allow Git to look inside the top-level parent directories
!/resources/
!/public/

# 3. Ignore everything inside those parent directories by default
/resources/*
/public/*

# 4. Allow Git to look inside the next level of subdirectories
!/resources/views/
!/public/assets/

# 5. Ignore everything inside those subdirectories by default
/resources/views/*
/public/assets/*

# 6. Allow Git to look inside the layout folder
!/resources/views/layouts/

# 7. Ignore everything inside layouts by default
/resources/views/layouts/*

# 8. Explicitly whitelist and track your target 'sigma' folders
!/resources/views/layouts/sigma/
!/public/assets/sigma/

# 9. Ensure your .gitignore file itself stays tracked
!.gitignore
```

## Check Your Setup
Run this terminal command in your project root to confirm Git sees the correct folders:

```bash
git status
```

<FollowUp>
Are you seeing any **tracked files from the ignored folders** showing up when you run that status check?
</FollowUp>
